WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.779
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.779 --> 00:00:10.840
In this series, we often discuss that neural
networks are extraordinarily useful for classification

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:11.840
tasks.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:16.290
This means that if we give them an image,
they can tell us what's on it, which is great

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:21.070
for self-driving cars, image search, and a
variety of other applications.

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:26.619
However, fewer people know that they can also
be used for image generation.

00:00:26.619 --> 00:00:32.630
We've seen many great examples of this where
NVIDIA's AI was able to dream up high-resolution

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:35.510
images of imaginary celebrities.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:40.630
This was done using a generative adversarial
network, an architecture where two neural

00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:42.630
networks battle each other.

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:48.640
However, these methods don't work too well
if we have too much variation in our datasets.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:54.450
For instance, they are great for faces, but
not for synthesizing an entire human body.

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:59.440
This particular technique uses a different
architecture, and as a result, can synthesize

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:06.270
an entire human body, and is also able to
synthesize both shape and appearance.

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:10.740
You will see in a moment that because of that,
it can do magical things.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:16.180
For instance, in this example, all we have
is one low-quality image of a test subject

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:20.180
as an input, and we can give it a photo of
a different person.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:25.810
What happens now is that the algorithm runs
pose estimation on this input, and transforms

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:28.290
our test subject into that pose.

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:33.180
The crazy thing about this is that it even
creates views for new angles we didn't even

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:36.320
have access to!

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:39.390
In this other experiment, we have one image
on the left.

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:45.630
What we can do here is that we specify not
a person, but draw the pose directly, indicating

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:51.210
that we wish to see our test subject in this
pose, and the algorithm is also able to create

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:52.860
an appropriate new image.

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:58.310
And again, it works for angles that require
information that we don't have access to.

00:01:58.310 --> 00:02:04.580
These new angles show that the technique understands
the concept of shorts or trousers...although

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:07.330
it seems to forget to put on socks sometimes.

00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:10.259
Truth be told, I don't blame it.

00:02:10.259 --> 00:02:15.640
What is even cooler is that it seems to behave
very similarly for a variety of different

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:16.670
inputs.

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:21.660
This is non-trivial as this property doesn't
just emerge out of thin air, and will be a

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:24.190
great selling point for this new method.

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:29.420
It also supports a feature where we need to
give a crude drawing to the algorithm, and

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:32.470
it will transform it into a photorealistic
image.

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:37.530
However, it is clear that there are many-many
ways to fill this drawing with information,

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:41.540
so how do we tell the algorithm what appearance
we are looking for?

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:46.810
Well, worry not, because this technique can
also perform appearance transfer.

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:51.950
This means that we can exert artistic control
over the output by providing a photo of a

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:57.450
different object, and it will transfer the
style of this photo to our input.

00:02:57.450 --> 00:03:02.630
No artistic skills needed, but good taste
is still as much of a necessity as ever.

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:07.780
Yet another AI that will empower both experts
and novice users alike.

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:12.310
And while we are enjoying these amazing results,
or even better, if you have already built

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:17.640
